WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.400
-Ivanka Trump tried
to distance herself

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.033
from her father and her family's
business during her testimony

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.601
in the New York fraud
trial this week,

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.501
and yet, Trump himself
remains far ahead.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:12.334
And the GOP also ran
to gather for a fiery

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.167
and mostly pointless debate
last night.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.968
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:20.300
♪♪

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.000
Donald Trump is far and away the
front runner in the GOP primary.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.834
He's 40 points ahead
of his nearest rival.

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:27.901
If you combine all his rivals,
Trump would still win.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:30.601
Trump is so dominant, even his
own former vice president,

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.534
who in a normal world
might be a top contender,

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.334
just dropped out last month
and nobody noticed or cared.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.534
Although,
I'm not sure anyone

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.534
has ever really noticed
Mike Pence.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.267
He's the - He's the color
they paint your apartment

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.934
before you move in.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.734
That's how he got away
from the mob

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.334
trying to kill him
on January 6th.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:51.634
He just stood on a pedestal
in the rotunda

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.167
and they thought
he was a statue.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.267
He's lucky that one guy
didn't try to steal him.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:02.400
So there's really no point
to continuing to hold

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.801
J.V. debates with
all the eventual losers.

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:06.400
The only real benefit
to these debates

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.167
is that wherever desperate
losers gather,

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.868
there's occasionally
some fireworks.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.868
Take, for example,
entrepreneur Vivek Ramaswamy --

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:16.067
you know, the guy with the
energy of a Hollywood assistant

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.200
who offers you a Fiji water
while you wait,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.934
and then tells his boss
you demanded a Fiji water.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.367
He's the guy in a zombie movie

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.534
who says he'll get the car
and come back for everyone else,

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.567
and then he just leaves
and drives off.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:28.734
But the joke's on him

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.267
because there's a zombie
in the back seat,

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.667
and when that zombie lunges
forward and bites his neck

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.467
while he screams
singing "Life Is a Highway,"

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.234
the whole audience cheers
with delight

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.534
because [bleep] that guy.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.133
Ramaswamy got into a heated
exchange with Nikki Haley,

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.400
who served as UN ambassador
under Donald Trump.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.467
You don't really need to know
what this is about

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.000
because it's all
weirdo nonsense.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.701
Except that Ramaswamy
attacked Haley's daughter

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.801
for using TikTok, and Haley
was fired up.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.334
-In the last debate,
she made fun of me

00:01:57.334 --> 00:02:00.167
for actually joining TikTok
while her own daughter

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:01.934
was actually using the app
for a long time.

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.667
So you might want to take care
of your family first.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.667
-Leave my daughter
out of your voice.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:09.133
-The next generation
of Americans are using it...

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:10.434
[ Audience booing ]
...and that's

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:11.567
actually the point.

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:13.501
You have her supporters
propping her up.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:16.467
That's fine. Here's the truth.
-You're just scum.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.667
-Ramaswamy elicited
a reaction from me

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.300
that I thought was impossible
when he said,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.100
"You might want to take care
of your family first."

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.167
I actually thought,
"Donald Trump would never!"

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.567
I mean, I'm kidding.
Of course he would.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:32.300
Scum, though, scum is not a word
you tend to hear

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.467
in a lofty political debate.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.467
I don't recall Lincoln
ever calling Douglas

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:38.300
a mouthy son of a bitch,
but let's face it,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.367
this is just
what the modern GOP is:

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.100
people attacking
other people's children

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.834
in the hopes of winning an
election they've already lost.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.868
At the next debate, I wouldn't
be shocked if Chris Christie

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.434
just broke a glass bottle
on the podium

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:51.067
and said, "You want to go?!
Let's go!"

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.767
This whole thing was
a demented circus.

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:53.968
Compare that
to the other side.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.501
I'm pretty sure
the most impolite thing

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.567
that ever happened
in a Democratic primary debate

00:02:57.567 --> 00:03:01.601
was Bernie putting
both fingers up in the air.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.067
Everyone was like,
"Whoa, whoa, Bernie!

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.434
Put those things back
in their holsters!"

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.400
"I'm keeping them both up!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.100
And if you wonder
why I hold them for,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.033
you can distribute them
equal amongst themselves!"

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.267
So you've got candidates
attacking each other's kids,

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:15.501
calling each other scum.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:16.901
Meanwhile, Ron DeSantis
is just standing there

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:18.434
in the middle of it,
getting overshadowed

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:22.868
and just making weird faces
while other people talk,

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.667
I guess not realizing
he is on camera.

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:28.267
And the only thing stranger than
that is his complete inability

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:32.067
to smile like
a normal human being.

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:33.767
If you're trying
to convince people

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.601
that you don't wear lifts
inside your boots,

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.567
maybe don't make the
"my heels are killing me" face.

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:40.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:42.501
Apparently he tried
to improve on

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.701
the off-putting smile he made
at the last debate,

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:47.167
but the big note he got
this time was "more tongue."

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:48.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.200
What's wrong with this guy?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.067
How did anyone ever think this
was the GOP's next great hope?

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:00.667
He's anti-woke, and he has
Fire Marshall Bill face.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:03.834
So, last night
went off the rails.

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:05.634
Or, rather,
there were never any rails.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:08.234
Going into the debate,
Ramaswamy actually said

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.367
his goal, in order
to appeal to GOP voters,

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.033
was to act like a lunatic.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:15.801
-I asked him what his campaign
strategy, his debate strategy

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.234
was going to be for tonight.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:20.334
He needs something to shake
loose, to break through.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:22.067
He said he wanted
to be unhinged.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:25.634
-I'm sorry. Your debate
strategy...was to be unhinged?

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:27.167
That's not a strategy
for a debate.

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.901
That's a strategy
for getting an entire row

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.300
to yourself on the subway.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.367
"I'll just wear
an astronaut helmet,

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.100
no pants, tell everyone
when the cockroaches

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.234
are actually CIA spies
who can read my mind,

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:39.400
and then I'll just put up
my feet and relax.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.367
Who's scum now?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.400
There was one thing they all
seemed to agree on, though.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.801
They are tired of losing.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.067
Thanks in large part to Trump,

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.033
the GOP has lost elections
in 2018,

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.400
2020, 2022
and then again this week,

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.901
and the candidates on stage
were fed up with it.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.634
-He said Republicans were
going to get tired of winning.

00:04:56.634 --> 00:05:00.367
Well, we saw last night,
I'm sick of Republicans losing.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:01.901
-I think there's something
deeper going on

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.167
in the Republican Party here,

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:06.200
and I am upset about
what happened last night.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.033
We've become a party of losers.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.734
-And you can believe them
when they say that

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:11.734
because they were
at the loser debate.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.434
And yet most of these losers
who are tired of losing

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.434
still say they'd vote
for perennial loser Trump

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:19.267
if he's the nominee,
which, as of this moment

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:21.934
is most likely going to be
the outcome by a mile.

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:23.734
In fact, Trump has taken
to belittling

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:25.033
his so-called opponents

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.234
and making fun of just
how far behind him they are,

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:28.434
like Ron DeSantis.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:30.501
He's coming up with
strange new metaphors

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:33.634
to explain what exactly happened
to DeSantis.

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:35.100
-You know that I endorsed Ron,

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.033
and he went from
having very little

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.734
to having a lot
and got him elected.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:43.033
He said, "They like you
in Florida, sir, very much.

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.601
I think that I could..."

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:46.067
Tears flowing from his eyes.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.100
[ Laughter ]
It's true.

00:05:49.767 --> 00:05:51.067
"I need your endorsement, sir.

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:53.067
I need your endorsement,
please."

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:54.567
They said,
"Governor, you're gonna run

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:55.767
against the president."

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:58.601
He said, "I have no comment!

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:01.334
I have no comment."
I said, "Wow, no comment?

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:04.467
That means he's going
to run to me."

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:07.601
And I said,
"Let's hit him hard right now."

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:09.534
And my people said, "Sir,
don't hit him.

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:10.834
He's a Republican."

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.968
I said, "I don't care
if he's a Republican,"

00:06:12.968 --> 00:06:16.234
and we hit him hard,
and now he's like a wounded,

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:17.968
falling bird from the sky.

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:22.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:25.801
-I -- I like
this new poetic Trump.

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:27.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:29.901
He should do his next rally
at a public reading

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:31.868
in the East Village.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:35.200
"He's like a wounded,
falling bird from the sky.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.167
And through the air
he doth pass by...

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.734
beating his wings to no avail.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:44.634
Upon these wings,
he once did sail...

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:48.234
from under heaven
to ashen earth...

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:50.534
ending in death
where he began in birth.

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:52.133
And so I said once he was gone,

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:53.534
'Here lies...

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.767
sad little...Meatball Ron.'"

00:06:55.767 --> 00:06:59.000
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.834
Trump, of course, is dealing
with his own set of problems,

00:07:01.834 --> 00:07:03.901
like his indictments, which he
complained about yet again

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:05.701
during a competing rally held

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:06.968
during last night's
loser debate.

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:09.834
Although, he's also come up
with a new twist

00:07:09.834 --> 00:07:11.601
on his indictment rant as well.

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:14.000
-Every time
the radical left Democrats,

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Marxists, communists
and fascists indict me --

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.400
They indicted me!
Can you believe? --

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.534
my father and mother
are looking down,

00:07:21.534 --> 00:07:23.667
"Son, how did that happen?

00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:26.534
We're so proud of you, son.
How did that happen?"

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:27.901
-"We're so proud of you."

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:31.834
Trump even makes dead people
say nice things about him.

00:07:31.834 --> 00:07:33.400
"The other day,
a ghost came up to me --

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.000
big ghost, dead ghost,

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.901
see-through tears
flowing down his spectral face

00:07:37.901 --> 00:07:39.868
and onto his jangling chains --

00:07:39.868 --> 00:07:42.033
and he said to me, 'Sir,
I owe you an apology, sir.

00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:44.801
Me and all my dead friends
in Pennsylvania

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:47.801
voted for Joe Biden.'"

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:49.234
"The Washington Post"
reported this week

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:52.200
that Trump apparently has a plan
in place to punish critics

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.000
and get revenge using
the Justice Department

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.234
if he wins another term.

00:07:55.234 --> 00:07:57.567
And at his rallies,
he's been announcing

00:07:57.567 --> 00:07:59.901
that he'll go after Joe Biden
for unspecified crimes.

00:07:59.901 --> 00:08:03.801
Although, he can't even say
what Biden supposedly did

00:08:03.801 --> 00:08:05.801
or what laws
he supposedly broke.

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:09.601
-We will start by exposing
every last crime committed

00:08:09.601 --> 00:08:13.801
by crooked Joe Biden,
because now that he indicted me,

00:08:13.801 --> 00:08:16.534
we're allowed to look at him.

00:08:16.534 --> 00:08:19.200
But he did real bad things.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.834
-Well, so much for poet Trump.

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.033
Guess he had
"Gilligan's Island" syndrome,

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:26.367
where a coconut fell on his head
and he became smart for a day,

00:08:26.367 --> 00:08:28.400
then another coconut
fell on his head

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.367
and he went back
to talking like a moron.

00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:34.767
"He did real bad things.
He's a...bad man. Fire bad."

00:08:34.767 --> 00:08:36.634
Of course, Trump is angry

00:08:36.634 --> 00:08:38.133
not just about
the four indictments,

00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:39.934
but also the civil fraud trial
in New York,

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:42.100
which threatens to wipe out
his entire business empire.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.300
Yesterday, his daughter Ivanka
testified and, unlike Trump

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.567
who threw a temper tantrum
and also at one point

00:08:47.567 --> 00:08:50.033
basically confessed to adjusting
the value of his assets,

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:51.901
Ivanka was very evasive.

00:08:51.901 --> 00:08:53.801
-The questions have
focused on her time

00:08:53.801 --> 00:08:55.367
at the Trump Organization.

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:57.467
She left the family business
in 2017

00:08:57.467 --> 00:08:59.200
when she went
to the White House.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.400
But the government has been
asking her questions

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.868
about specific projects that she
worked on while she was there.

00:09:04.868 --> 00:09:07.234
-Ivanka Trump testifying
that she had no role

00:09:07.234 --> 00:09:09.367
in her father's personal
financial statements.

00:09:09.367 --> 00:09:12.033
-Ivanka Trump saying
at least 30 times

00:09:12.033 --> 00:09:15.167
she does not recall details
about e-mails, meetings,

00:09:15.167 --> 00:09:18.767
conversations or documents
from her time with the company.

00:09:18.767 --> 00:09:20.767
-I expect that she
is going to try to do

00:09:20.767 --> 00:09:23.767
as little as possible
to inflame her father,

00:09:23.767 --> 00:09:26.567
but also to distance herself
from any --

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:28.801
any questions
that the AG would have.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:31.601
-Oh, come on, you can't
distance yourself from him now.

00:09:31.601 --> 00:09:34.067
You campaigned for him, worked
in the White House with him,

00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:36.601
you sat next to him
at the boardroom table.

00:09:36.601 --> 00:09:38.567
You can't suddenly say,
"I wasn't involved.

00:09:38.567 --> 00:09:39.534
All I know is..."

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:41.901
-He did real bad things.

00:09:41.901 --> 00:09:44.968
-Trying to distance yourself
from your father now is absurd.

00:09:44.968 --> 00:09:47.734
The only distance between Ivanka
and her father is the distance

00:09:47.734 --> 00:09:49.667
between the quality
of their courtroom sketches.

00:09:49.667 --> 00:09:50.801
Here's an Ivanka sketch,

00:09:50.801 --> 00:09:53.200
which seems like
a reasonably fair depiction.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.968
Now, compare that
to Trump's sketch.

00:09:54.968 --> 00:09:57.033
Yah!
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.033 --> 00:09:59.300
He looks like one
of those freaky little demons

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.801
from a Hieronymus Bosch
painting.

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:03.934
I almost feel like whoever
did that Ivanka sketch

00:10:03.934 --> 00:10:06.067
made sure to do a good job
just to make Trump's look

00:10:06.067 --> 00:10:07.901
even worse by comparison.

00:10:07.901 --> 00:10:09.434
They even gave her papers
to read.

00:10:09.434 --> 00:10:11.167
They might as well have also
given her a word bubble

00:10:11.167 --> 00:10:13.367
that says "I'm smart"
and given him a dunce cap.

00:10:13.367 --> 00:10:15.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:15.133 --> 00:10:18.067
The self-professed party losers
lost big yet again on Tuesday,

00:10:18.067 --> 00:10:20.100
and they're all angry about it,
but they have no solutions.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.634
Their front runner
is still Donald Trump,

00:10:21.634 --> 00:10:23.300
who's still facing
four criminal cases

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.868
and is still very unpopular
outside of the Republican Party.

00:10:25.868 --> 00:10:27.400
That doesn't mean he can't win,

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.734
but if he loses
and he gets convicted,

00:10:29.734 --> 00:10:31.300
there's a good chance
we will finally see...

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:32.968
-Tears flowing from his eyes.

00:10:32.968 --> 00:10:34.734
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:34.734 --> 00:10:38.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:38.767 --> 00:10:40.667
Hey, everybody. Thanks
for watching "A Closer Look."

00:10:40.667 --> 00:10:42.634
And as a reminder,
my brother, Josh, and I

00:10:42.634 --> 00:10:44.400
have started a new podcast

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.033
called "Family Trips
with the Meyers Brothers."

00:10:47.033 --> 00:10:49.801
We hope you listen, we hope
you like it, and see you soon.

